nals/output":"1941-01-22","later-events_catalog":"1941-01-22","stage19_causal_queue":"1941-01-22"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:8647","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"it is ordered that all lands owned by the United States within the following-described areas, comprising approximately 37,370 acres, in Mohave and Yuma Counties, Arizona, and San Bernardino County, California, be, and they are hereby, reserved and set apart, subject to valid existing rights, for the use of the Department of the Interior as a refuge and breeding ground for migratory birds and other wildlife; and all lands hereafter acquired by the United States within such areas, including tribal and allotted Indian lands in which complete interests may hereafter be acquired by the United States pursuant to the act of July 8, 1940, Public No. 730, shall upon acquisition thereof become and be reserved as a part of the said refuge:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372520; common-crawl capture 2025-05-15T23:37:24Z; unnumbered paragraph 1","sha256":"d8fa531bc7bd803007a8a1979c8674198988b78834da6e78c36e26ea01f1d87a","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-8647-establishing-the-havasu-lake-national-wildlife-refuge"},"scope_id":"EO:8647#p1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"As the lands herein described have been reserved or acquired, or are to be acquired, for purposes of the Parker Dam Project, their reservation as the Havasu Lake National Wildlife Refuge is subject to their use for the purposes of the Parker Dam Project.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372520; common-crawl capture 2025-05-15T23:37:24Z; unnumbered paragraph 2","sha256":"d8fa531bc7bd803007a8a1979c8674198988b78834da6e78c36e26ea01f1d87a","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-8647-establishing-the-havasu-lake-national-wildlife-refuge"},"scope_id":"EO:8647#p2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"It is unlawful for any person to pursue, hunt, trap, capture, willfully disturb, or kill any bird or wild animal of any kind whatsoever within the limits of the refuge, or to enter thereon, except under such rules and regulations as may be prescribed by the Secretary of the Interior.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372520; common-crawl capture 2025-05-15T23:37:24Z; unnumbered paragraph 3","sha256":"d8fa531bc7bd803007a8a1979c8674198988b78834da6e78c36e26ea01f1d87a","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-8647-establishing-the-havasu-lake-national-wildlife-refuge"},"scope_id":"EO:8647#p3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"This reservation shall be known as the Havasu Lake National Wildlife Refuge.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372520; common-crawl capture 2025-05-15T23:37:24Z; unnumbered paragraph 4","sha256":"d8fa531bc7bd803007a8a1979c8674198988b78834da6e78c36e26ea01f1d87a","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-8647-establishing-the-havasu-lake-national-wildlife-refuge"},"scope_id":"EO:8647#p4","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":null,"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: original_representation not yet confir